%%{init: {"theme": "base", "flowchart": {"nodeSpacing": 30, "rankSpacing": 40, "curve": "linear", "diagramPadding": 10}}}%%
%% How the goal works in Muse — compact, GitHub-readable.
%% Styled to match the PNG: plain white boxes, black borders,
%% green highlight on the auto-inferred goal. The PNG is the
%% full-detail version (same structure, longer notes).
%% Muse sets the goal AUTOMATICALLY: it infers the goal from the
%% project/conversation and declares it itself (docs/goals.md, system
%% prompt, goal-mechanism-spec.md lines 9/50). No set-goal command
%% from Den. From the design description + Muse's goal docs —
%% NOT from Muse internals. Do not read more into it.
%% Detail lives in muse-goal-mechanism.md.
%% NOTE: Mermaid decides node positions itself (dagre layout).
%% This file controls boxes, labels, edges, colours, and spacing —
%% not exact coordinates. The PNG keeps the exact sketch geometry.

flowchart TD
    classDef plain fill:#fff,stroke:#000,stroke-width:2px,color:#000
    classDef hl fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#000,stroke-width:3px,color:#000

    AUTO("★ Muse sets the goal AUTOMATICALLY"):::hl
    SUP("Supervisor — hourly, re-asserts the goal"):::plain
    PICK("Picks next UNBLOCKED card"):::plain
    BUILD("Subagent builds the card"):::plain
    UPD("Subagent updates the board"):::plain
    BOARD("Board"):::plain
    NOTE("No set-goal command from Den · hourly only, no idle trigger"):::plain

    AUTO --> SUP
    SUP --> PICK
    PICK --> BUILD
    BUILD --> UPD
    UPD --> SUP
    PICK --> BOARD
    UPD --> BOARD
    AUTO -.- NOTE
